> integrate exp(-x^2) from -inf to inf numerically qmc
∫ exp(-x^2) numerically, x from -inf to inf
  quasi-Monte Carlo (an estimate, not a proof): 1.772453851, standard error 7.1e-16
    8 randomised replicates of 4096 Sobol points in 1 dimension (Joe-Kuo direction numbers, a random digital shift each; seed 1)
    infinite sides onto t in [0, 1), the integrand times the derivative: x = s/(1 - s^2), s = 2t - 1, for the whole line
    the error is estimated from the 8 replicates' spread: +-1.7e-15 at 95% if their means are normal (t = 2.365), which nothing proves
